From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:11:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] A shaft of daylight from each window, lit by the window itself

Patch 0051 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-09: "can you add the beam back in in the temple of time since we now aligned the
light?", and then, preferring it: "make our own visible light that starts at window and fades
closer to the floor but looks way more natural and uses actual lighting somehow".

The air pass (ScatterRayGen) gains the windows' shafts (windowShafts). Each window light knows its
glass and the way its daylight falls, so its beam is the glass's outline pushed along that
direction. For each window the stretch of the pixel's ray inside the beam is found exactly (each
bound is linear along the ray) and marched in ShaftSteps jittered points; at each, the window's own
soft edged outline, a fade with the distance from the glass (exp of travel over the Shaft length),
and one shadow ray back toward the glass, so a pillar in the beam cuts a gap through the air. The
light is the window's own. tuneShafts, a new parameter group: x the Window shafts row (0 off), y the
Shaft length, z the Debugging menu's Drawn beam row, read on the CPU, which shows the game's painted
beam again where 0034/0039 hide it.

diff --git a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
--- a/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
+++ b/src/shaders/Raytracing.hlsl
@@ -1843,6 +1843,119 @@ float3 dustInLight(float3 origin, float3 direction, float end, uint2 launchIndex
     return sum;
 }
 
+// A SHAFT OF DAYLIGHT FROM EACH WINDOW, LIT BY THE WINDOW ITSELF (patch 0051, the user, 2026-10-09:
+// "can you add the beam back in in the temple of time since we now aligned the light?", and then,
+// preferring it: "make our own visible light that starts at window and fades closer to the floor
+// but looks way more natural and uses actual lighting somehow").
+//
+// The game paints one beam, a fading cylinder that lights nothing, and 0034/0039 hide it while the
+// windows give traced light. This is the air the windows' own light passes through. Each window
+// is a light that knows its glass (its middle, its inward normal, its half width and height, the
+// pointed top) and the way its daylight falls, so the beam it makes is the glass's outline pushed
+// along that direction: a point is in the shaft when the light reaching it came through the glass.
+//
+// For each window, the stretch of this pixel's ray that lies inside its beam is found exactly (the
+// beam is the glass pushed along the light, so each bound is linear along the ray), and only that
+// stretch is marched, ShaftSteps points jittered by the blue noise. At each, the same soft edged
+// outline the window lights surfaces with, a fade with how far the light has come from the glass,
+// and one shadow ray back up toward the glass, so a pillar standing in the beam cuts a dark gap
+// through the air below it. The light is the window's own color and strength.
+//
+// The Window shafts row (tuneShafts.x, 0 off) scales the air's brightness per world unit of beam
+// crossed, and the Shaft length row (tuneShafts.y) is the distance from the glass over which the
+// shaft fades to about a third. Nothing here touches the light on surfaces.
+static const uint ShaftSteps = 12;
+static const float ShaftFadeReach = 5.0f;   // past this many fade lengths a shaft is not marched at all
+
+// Narrows [t0, t1] to where a + b t lies within [lo, hi].
+void clipShaftSlab(float a, float b, float lo, float hi, inout float t0, inout float t1) {
+    if (abs(b) < 1.0e-6f) {
+        if ((a < lo) || (a > hi)) {
+            t1 = -1.0f;
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
+    const float ta = (lo - a) / b;
+    const float tb = (hi - a) / b;
+    t0 = max(t0, min(ta, tb));
+    t1 = min(t1, max(ta, tb));
+}
+
+float3 windowShafts(float3 origin, float3 direction, float end, float jitter) {
+    const float strength = RtParams.tuneShafts.x;
+    if (strength <= 0.0f) {
+        return float3(0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
+    }
+
+    const float shaftLength = max(RtParams.tuneShafts.y, 50.0f);
+    const uint count = min(RtParams.lightsCount, RtParams.maxLights);
+    float3 sum = 0.0f;
+    for (uint i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+        const PointLight light = SceneLights[i];
+        if ((light.groupBits & WindowLightBit) == 0u) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        const float3 falls = light.direction;
+        const float3 inward = light.specularColor;
+        const float approach = dot(falls, inward);
+        if (approach <= 0.05f) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        // The ray in the window's own terms: how far inside the glass's plane a point is (i0 + i1 t),
+        // and where on the glass the light reaching it came through (A + B t).
+        const float3 across = normalize(cross(float3(0.0f, 1.0f, 0.0f), inward));
+        const float3 rel = origin - light.position;
+        const float i0 = dot(rel, inward);
+        const float i1 = dot(direction, inward);
+        const float3 onGlassA = rel - falls * (i0 / approach);
+        const float3 onGlassB = direction - falls * (i1 / approach);
+        const float reach = ShaftFadeReach * shaftLength;
+        const float margin = 2.0f + WindowEdge * reach;
+        float t0 = 0.0f;
+        float t1 = end;
+        clipShaftSlab(i0, i1, WindowGlassDepth, reach * approach, t0, t1);
+        clipShaftSlab(dot(onGlassA, across), dot(onGlassB, across), -light.pointRadius - margin, light.pointRadius + margin, t0, t1);
+        clipShaftSlab(onGlassA.y, onGlassB.y, -light.spotMaxCosine - margin, light.spotMaxCosine + margin, t0, t1);
+        if (t1 <= t0) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        const float stepLength = (t1 - t0) / float(ShaftSteps);
+        float lit = 0.0f;
+        for (uint s = 0; s < ShaftSteps; s++) {
+            const float t = t0 + (float(s) + jitter) * stepLength;
+            const float3 p = origin + direction * t;
+            const float inside = dot(p - light.position, inward);
+            if (inside <= WindowGlassDepth) {
+                continue;
+            }
+
+            const float travel = inside / approach;
+            const float3 offset = (p - falls * travel) - light.position;
+            const float edge = WindowEdge * travel + 2.0f;
+            const float openWidth = windowOpenWidth(light, offset.y);
+            const float acrossShare = 1.0f - smoothstep(openWidth - edge, openWidth + edge, abs(dot(offset, across)));
+            const float upShare = 1.0f - smoothstep(light.spotMaxCosine - edge, light.spotMaxCosine + edge, abs(offset.y));
+            const float share = acrossShare * upShare;
+            if (share <= 0.0f) {
+                continue;
+            }
+
+            const float tMax = max(travel - WindowClearance, 0.0f);
+            float hitDistance;
+            const float visible = (tMax > 1.0f) ? traceVisibilityRange(p, -falls, 0.0f, tMax, hitDistance) : 1.0f;
+            lit += share * exp(-travel / shaftLength) * visible;
+        }
+
+        sum += light.diffuseColor * (lit * stepLength);
+    }
+
+    return sum * strength;
+}
+
 [shader("raygeneration")]
 void ScatterRayGen() {
     const uint2 launchIndex = DispatchRaysIndex().xy;
@@ -1882,7 +1995,8 @@ void ScatterRayGen() {
     const float sunHaze = RtParams.tuneScatter.y;
     const float fadeEnd = max(RtParams.tuneScatter.z, 10.0f);
     const float fadeStart = fadeEnd * 0.35f;
-    if ((lightGlow <= 0.0f) && (sunHaze <= 0.0f) && !dust) {
+    const bool shafts = (RtParams.tuneShafts.x > 0.0f);   // the windows' shafts (patch 0051)
+    if ((lightGlow <= 0.0f) && (sunHaze <= 0.0f) && !dust && !shafts) {
         gScatter[launchIndex] = 0.0f;
         return;
     }
@@ -1978,6 +2092,12 @@ void ScatterRayGen() {
         sum += dustInLight(origin, direction, end, launchIndex, dustDensity, dustVisibility, dustSize, outdoors);
     }
 
+    // The windows' shafts (patch 0051), as far as the surface this pixel shows: a tall hall is
+    // deeper than the air's own range.
+    if (shafts) {
+        sum += windowShafts(origin, direction, min(length(gShadingPosition[launchIndex].xyz - origin), 8000.0f), noise.y);
+    }
+
     // No history here (patch 0008): the glow is smooth on its own and follows a moving light
     // (Navi), and a history of it painted a trail behind her.
     gScatter[launchIndex] = float4(sum, 1.0f);
